---
import SEOLayout from '../layouts/SEOLayout.astro';
const title = "What is a Webhook? The Ultimate Guide for Developers (2026)";
const description = "Learn exactly what a webhook is, how it works, and how it differs from APIs. A comprehensive guide with diagrams, code examples in Node/Python/PHP, and security best practices.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": title,
  "description": description,
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Sudarshan Chavan"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "WebhookCatch",
    "logo": {
      "@type": "ImageObject",
      "url": "https://webhookcatch.com/favicon.svg"
    }
  }
};
---

<SEOLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>

  <main class="guide-layout">
    <div class="guide-container">
      
      <!-- Table of Contents Sidebar -->
      <aside class="guide-sidebar hidden-mobile">
        <div class="toc-sticky">
          <h4 class="text-caption" style="color: var(--color-mute); margin-bottom: 16px; text-transform: uppercase;">Table of Contents</h4>
          <ul class="toc-list">
            <li><a href="#introduction">What is a Webhook?</a></li>
            <li><a href="#how-it-works">How Webhooks Work</a></li>
            <li><a href="#api-vs-webhook">API Polling vs Webhooks</a></li>
            <li><a href="#code-examples">How to Receive Webhooks (Code)</a></li>
            <li><a href="#security">Security & Reliability</a></li>
            <li><a href="#testing">Testing Webhooks Locally</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <!-- Main Content -->
      <article class="guide-content">
        
        <!-- Header -->
        <header style="margin-bottom: 64px;">
          <div class="badge" style="display: inline-block; padding: 4px 12px; background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); border-radius: 16px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--color-mute); margin-bottom: 16px;">
            Developer Guides
          </div>
          <h1 class="text-display" style="font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 24px; letter-spacing: -1px;">
            What is a <span style="color: var(--color-primary);">Webhook?</span><br/>The Ultimate Guide.
          </h1>
          <p class="text-body-lg" style="color: var(--color-body); max-width: 600px; font-size: 20px; line-height: 32px;">
            A complete, visual breakdown of webhooks, how they differ from traditional APIs, and exactly how to implement them securely in your next project.
          </p>
        </header>

        <section id="introduction" style="margin-bottom: 64px;">
          <h2 class="text-heading-2" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">Introduction: The "Push" API</h2>
          <p class="text-body" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
            At its core, a <strong>webhook</strong> (sometimes called a web callback or an HTTP push API) is a way for one application to send real-time data to another application as soon as a specific event happens.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
            Instead of requiring you to constantly ask a server, "Did the user pay yet? Did they pay yet?", a webhook flips the script. You give the server a URL, and the server promises to send a message (usually a JSON payload) to that URL the exact millisecond the payment succeeds.
          </p>
          <div style="background: #f8fafc; border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary); padding: 24px; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; margin-top: 32px;">
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: #334155;">
              <strong>TL;DR:</strong> An API is when <em>you</em> call a server to pull data. A webhook is when a <em>server</em> calls your API to push data to you.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="how-it-works" style="margin-bottom: 64px;">
          <h2 class="text-heading-2" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">How does it actually work?</h2>
          <p class="text-body" style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
            The webhook flow consists of three main steps: the event, the payload, and your endpoint.
          </p>
          
          <div class="process-grid">
            <div class="process-card">
              <div class="process-num">1</div>
              <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 600;">The Trigger Event</h3>
              <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--color-body); line-height: 24px;">A customer successfully purchases a product on your Stripe checkout page.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="process-card">
              <div class="process-num">2</div>
              <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 600;">The Payload</h3>
              <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--color-body); line-height: 24px;">Stripe instantly packages the customer's payment details into a JSON object.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="process-card">
              <div class="process-num">3</div>
              <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 600;">The POST Request</h3>
              <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--color-body); line-height: 24px;">Stripe sends that JSON payload via an HTTP POST request to your designated webhook URL.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="api-vs-webhook" style="margin-bottom: 64px;">
          <h2 class="text-heading-2" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">API Polling vs. Webhooks</h2>
          <p class="text-body" style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
            Before webhooks, developers had to use "API Polling". This meant running a cron job every 60 seconds to ask the server if anything changed. This wasted massive amounts of bandwidth and computing power.
          </p>
          
          <div class="comparison-visual">
            <div class="comp-box polling">
              <h4 style="margin-bottom: 16px; font-size: 16px;">API Polling (Inefficient)</h4>
              <div class="anim-row">
                <span class="client">Your Server</span>
                <div class="anim-arrow">
                  <div class="arrow-line"></div>
                  <span style="font-size: 12px; background: white; padding: 0 4px; position: relative; z-index: 2;">"Any updates?"</span>
                </div>
                <span class="server">Stripe</span>
              </div>
              <div class="anim-row">
                <span class="client">Your Server</span>
                <div class="anim-arrow reverse">
                  <div class="arrow-line"></div>
                  <span style="font-size: 12px; background: white; padding: 0 4px; position: relative; z-index: 2;">"No."</span>
                </div>
                <span class="server">Stripe</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="comp-box webhook">
              <h4 style="margin-bottom: 16px; font-size: 16px;">Webhooks (Real-time)</h4>
              <div class="anim-row" style="margin-top: 24px;">
                <span class="client">Your Server</span>
                <div class="anim-arrow reverse success">
                  <div class="arrow-line"></div>
                  <span style="font-size: 12px; background: #f0fdf4; padding: 0 4px; position: relative; z-index: 2; color: #166534;">"Hey! A payment succeeded! Here is the data."</span>
                </div>
                <span class="server">Stripe</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="code-examples" style="margin-bottom: 64px;">
          <h2 class="text-heading-2" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">How to Receive a Webhook</h2>
          <p class="text-body" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
            To receive a webhook, you just need to create an open HTTP endpoint on your server that accepts `POST` requests. Here are simple examples in various languages:
          </p>

          <div class="code-tabs">
            <div class="tabs-header">
              <button class="tab-btn active" data-target="code-node">Node.js (Express)</button>
              <button class="tab-btn" data-target="code-python">Python (Flask)</button>
              <button class="tab-btn" data-target="code-php">PHP</button>
            </div>
            
            <div class="tab-content active" id="code-node">
<pre is:raw style="margin:0; padding: 24px; background: #1e293b; color: #e2e8f0; border-radius: 0 0 8px 8px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

// This is your webhook endpoint
app.post('/webhook', (req, res) => {
  const payload = req.body;
  console.log('Webhook received!', payload);
  
  // You must return a 2xx status code quickly!
  res.status(200).send('Webhook processed successfully');
});

app.listen(3000, () => console.log('Listening on port 3000'));</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="tab-content" id="code-python" style="display:none;">
<pre is:raw style="margin:0; padding: 24px; background: #1e293b; color: #e2e8f0; border-radius: 0 0 8px 8px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>from flask import Flask, request, jsonify
app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route('/webhook', methods=['POST'])
def webhook():
    payload = request.json
    print('Webhook received!', payload)
    
    # Return a 200 OK immediately
    return jsonify(success=True), 200

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(port=3000)</code></pre>
            </div>
            
            <div class="tab-content" id="code-php" style="display:none;">
<pre is:raw style="margin:0; padding: 24px; background: #1e293b; color: #e2e8f0; border-radius: 0 0 8px 8px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>&lt;?php
// Get the JSON payload
$payload = file_get_contents('php://input');
$data = json_decode($payload, true);

// Log or process the data
error_log('Webhook received: ' . $payload);

// Return 200 OK
http_response_code(200);
echo json_encode(["status" => "success"]);
?&gt;</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="security" style="margin-bottom: 64px;">
          <h2 class="text-heading-2" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">Webhook Security & Best Practices</h2>
          
          <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px;">
            <div style="background: var(--color-surface); padding: 24px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);">
              <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 600;">1. Verify Signatures (HMAC)</h3>
              <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--color-body); line-height: 24px;">Since your webhook URL is public, anyone can send fake requests to it. Providers (like GitHub or Stripe) include a cryptographic signature in the headers. You must verify this signature to ensure the request is actually from them.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div style="background: var(--color-surface); padding: 24px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);">
              <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 600;">2. Respond Quickly</h3>
              <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--color-body); line-height: 24px;">Providers require you to respond with a <code>200 OK</code> within seconds. If your processing takes a long time, save the data to a database queue, respond 200 immediately, and process it in the background.</p>
            </div>

            <div style="background: var(--color-surface); padding: 24px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);">
              <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 600;">3. Handle Retries Safely</h3>
              <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--color-body); line-height: 24px;">If your server crashes and fails to return a 200 OK, the provider will usually retry the webhook later. Make sure your logic is <strong>idempotent</strong>, meaning if you receive the exact same webhook twice, you don't double-charge a customer.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div style="background: var(--color-surface); padding: 24px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);">
              <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 600;">4. IP Whitelisting</h3>
              <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--color-body); line-height: 24px;">As an added layer of security, many providers publish a list of their exact IP addresses. You can configure your firewall to block any POST requests to your webhook URL that don't originate from those known IPs.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="testing" style="margin-bottom: 64px;">
          <h2 class="text-heading-2" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">Testing Webhooks Locally</h2>
          <p class="text-body" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
            The hardest part of building webhooks is testing them while your code is running on `localhost`. Providers like Stripe can't send requests to your local computer because it doesn't have a public IP address.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body" style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
            That's exactly why we built <a href="/" style="color: var(--color-primary); font-weight: 600;">WebhookCatch</a>. You can generate a free, public URL instantly, plug it into your provider, and inspect the incoming JSON payloads live.
          </p>
          <div style="text-align: center;">
            <a href="/" class="btn-primary" style="display: inline-flex; text-decoration: none;">Create a Free Webhook URL Now</a>
          </div>
        </section>

      </article>
    </div>
  </main>

  </SEOLayout>

<style>
  .guide-layout {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 80px 24px;
  }
  
  .guide-container {
    display: flex;
    gap: 64px;
    position: relative;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .guide-sidebar {
    width: 260px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .toc-sticky {
    position: sticky;
    top: 100px;
  }

  .toc-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .toc-list li {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .toc-list a {
    color: var(--color-body);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 15px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .toc-list a:hover {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .guide-content {
    flex-grow: 1;
    max-width: 800px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .process-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .process-card {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
    padding: 24px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    position: relative;
  }

  .process-num {
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    background: var(--color-primary);
    color: white;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  /* Comparison Visual */
  .comparison-visual {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .comp-box {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 32px;
  }

  .anim-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    position: relative;
  }

  .client, .server {
    background: var(--color-canvas);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline-strong);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 14px;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .anim-arrow {
    flex-grow: 1;
    margin: 0 16px;
    height: 2px;
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .arrow-line {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 2px;
    background: #cbd5e1;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
  }

  .arrow-line::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    right: 0;
    top: -4px;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-top: 2px solid #cbd5e1;
    border-right: 2px solid #cbd5e1;
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }

  .anim-arrow.reverse .arrow-line::after {
    right: auto;
    left: 0;
    border-top: none;
    border-right: none;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #cbd5e1;
    border-left: 2px solid #cbd5e1;
  }

  .anim-arrow.success .arrow-line {
    background: #22c55e;
  }
  .anim-arrow.success.reverse .arrow-line::after {
    border-bottom-color: #22c55e;
    border-left-color: #22c55e;
  }

  /* Tabs */
  .code-tabs {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .tabs-header {
    display: flex;
    background: #f1f5f9;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }

  .tab-btn {
    padding: 12px 24px;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-body);
    cursor: pointer;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }

  .tab-btn.active {
    background: #1e293b;
    color: white;
    border-color: #1e293b;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hidden-mobile {
      display: none;
    }
    .process-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .guide-container {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    .comparison-visual > div > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .guide-content section > div[style*="grid-template-columns"] {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Simple tab logic
  document.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      // Remove active from all buttons
      document.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
      // Hide all contents
      document.querySelectorAll('.tab-content').forEach(c => (c as HTMLElement).style.display = 'none');
      
      // Activate clicked
      btn.classList.add('active');
      const target = btn.getAttribute('data-target');
      if(target) document.getElementById(target).style.display = 'block';
    });
  });
</script>
